    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="0982" n="970" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg970"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.115A/1489: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-16">March 16, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>638. Your 1552, March 7th.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d834-f1"/> American interests,
                    Japan. Swiss should request Japanese authorities to install a canteen at Negishi
                    Yokohama Camp in accordance with the provisions of Article 12 of the Geneva
                    Prisoners of War Convention.</p>
                <p>The attention of the Swiss authorities should be again drawn to paragraph 2 of
                    Department’s 393 of February 15<anchor n="26" xml:id="d834-f2"/> with regard to
                    interviews between internees and Swiss delegate in the presence of
                    witnesses.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
